data: {"messages":[{"content":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"d7d8f4ef-6fb1-449d-95f4-d11cfedf7409"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-contract-review</name>\n      <description>中国合同审查 skill。\nUse this skill when the user provides a full contract text, a draft agreement,\nor concrete clauses and wants structured review on:\n- contract validity\n- rights and obligations\n- breach / default clauses\n- risk points\n- revision suggestions\n- dispute resolution clause risks\nDo NOT use this skill for full dispute analysis driven by case facts.\nIf the task is to analyze a dispute, identify claims/defenses, or build evidence strategy,\nuse china-legal-issue-analysis instead.\nIf the user only needs a lightweight initial consultation without clause-level review,\nuse china-legal-consultation.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-contract-review/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-legal-consultation</name>\n      <description>中国法律咨询 skill。\nUse this skill when a party describes a legal problem and mainly wants:\n- legal relationship explanation\n- risk reminders\n- rights-protection path guidance\n- evidence suggestions\n- practical notes / cautions\nDo NOT use this skill for full contract redlining or the full dispute-analysis path.\nIf the user needs full case analysis, use china-legal-issue-analysis.\nIf the user provides a full contract for clause review, use china-contract-review.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-legal-consultation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-legal-issue-analysis</name>\n      <description>中国法律问题分析 skill。\nUse this skill for concrete Chinese legal issues, dispute analysis,\nissue spotting, legal relationship analysis, risk assessment,\nlitigation/arbitration positioning, and action planning.\nCore capabilities:\n- case type identification\n- six-part checklist generation\n- 10-step legal analysis process\n- IRAC / claim-right / issue-based analysis\n- domain-specific issue analysis\n- legal citation verification and revision\nDo NOT use this skill as a dedicated contract redlining skill.\nIf the primary input is a full contract text that needs clause-by-clause review,\nuse china-contract-review instead.\nIf the user only needs a lightweight initial answer as a party to a dispute,\nuse china-legal-consultation instead.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-legal-issue-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>chinese-policy-analysis</name>\n      <description>This skill should be used when the user asks to \"分析中国政策\", \"评估政策落地可能性\", \"判断政策执行力度\", \"预判政策走向\", \"解读政策文件\", or needs systematic framework to analyze Chinese government policy implementation likelihood, execution paths, and actual impact.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/chinese-policy-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code2patent</name>\n      <description>从已开发代码项目中提取技术实现证据，围绕候选专利方案生成技术交底书，并以“权利要求布局卡 → 发明专利初稿”两步法继续生成接近可申报版的中国发明专利起草材料。触发场景包括：读取代码仓库后撰写技术交底书、将人工总结的专利方案映射到具体实现、从代码中挖掘可专利技术方案、为专利代理师准备权利要求布局和发明专利初稿。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/code2patent/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>law-local-retrieval</name>\n      <description>基于 Elasticsearch 的政策法规条文检索 Skill。适用于从已建立的政策法规 ES 索引中检索中国法律法规、政策文件、法律条文、政策依据、执法依据、效力状态、发布机关、发布日期、实施日期等信息，并为政策分析报告、合规审查、执法风险分析提供可回溯的法规依据。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/law-local-retrieval/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-briefing</name>\n      <description>中国法律材料整理、备忘录撰写与报告生成助手。\nThis skill is NOT the primary legal retrieval skill.\nUse it only after legal materials have already been retrieved, analyzed, or explicitly provided by the user.\nCore responsibilities:\n- organize already retrieved statutes, judicial interpretations, cases, and policy materials\n- turn existing legal materials into structured briefings, memos, summaries, and risk notes\n- compare multiple rules and explain their relationship in a concise, usable format\n- adapt output depth and style for different user roles\nDo NOT use this skill as the first-step legal retrieval skill for:\n- 查法条原文\n- 查第几条怎么规定\n- 查司法解释/法规/规范性文件\n- 询问“法律依据是什么”\n- 询问“根据什么法律”</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-briefing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-document-assistant</name>\n      <description>提供常见法律文书模板与撰写指导，涵盖劳务纠纷、离婚协议、交通事故、租房协议等场景；当用户需要法律文书模板、撰写建议或遇到法律纠纷时使用</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-document-assistant/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-proposal-generator</name>\n      <description>根据案件材料或沟通记录生成各类法律服务文档（诉讼方案、咨询报告、非诉方案、建议书、沟通报告、案件分析摘要等）。本技能应在用户需要将案件材料、咨询记录或沟通内容整理为专业法律文档时使用。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-proposal-generator/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-qa-extractor</name>\n      <description>从律师与客户沟通记录中提取有价值的法律问答对，生成结构化知识库内容。本技能应在用户需要整理客户咨询记录、从对话中提取可复用法律知识、创建问答知识库、或准备内容营销素材时使用。支持严格客户信息脱敏处理。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-qa-extractor/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-text-format</name>\n      <description>将法律文本（法律条文或法律案例）转换为规范的 Markdown 格式，删除推广冗余信息。本技能应在用户需要处理法律条文（如民法典、刑法等）、整理法律案例（如最高法典型案例、裁判文书等）、或从粘贴文本中格式化法律文档时使用。注意：本技能只负责格式化和内容清理，不包含内容抓取能力。内容获取应由其他 skill（如 wechat-article-fetch）完成，AI 会自动判断技能协作顺序。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-text-format/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>litigation-analysis</name>\n      <description>诉讼分析工具 - 判决书深度分析，生成上诉/再审决策支持</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/litigation-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>official-document-writer</name>\n      <description>Use this skill only when the user explicitly asks to draft, polish, revise, or export a formal Chinese official document such as 请示、报告、汇报材料、公文草拟. The skill should first gather authoritative policy basis from available web search/fetch tools or user-provided/local materials, then draft the document in formal official Chinese style. Do not use this skill for general policy Q&A, legal retrieval, ordinary article writing, or broad research tasks.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/official-document-writer/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>patent-analysis</name>\n      <description>当需要分析专利文件、进行侵权评估、提取技术特征、或比较多个专利的保护范围时使用。触发场景包括专利比对、权利要求分析、侵权检查、专利技术要点总结、专利稳定性分析、专利价值评估、FTO分析。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/patent-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>policy-rag</name>\n      <description>当用户需要处理企业内部制度文件、审批流程表、审批权责表，或需要基于内部制度与审批流进行检索、问答、索引构建时，使用本技能。适用于制度文档拆分、Excel 审批表转换、制度索引构建、制度条款检索、审批路径检索等场景。不适用于国家法律法规、司法解释、裁判案例等法律检索任务；此类问题应交由专门的法律检索技能处理。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/policy-rag/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>trademark-assistant</name>\n      <description>面向中国商标申请的类别规划、可注册性初筛及申请材料准备技能。基于尼斯分类（国际商标分类），引用中国法律法规。本技能应在接到商标咨询、需要结构化输出建议与风险分级、或需要准备申请材料时使用。不要用于：替代正式法律意见、承诺注册成功率、处理复杂商标争议案件。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/trademark-assistant/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>wechat-article-fetch</name>\n      <description>抓取微信公众号文章内容，使用 Playwright headless 模式无弹窗后台抓取，支持动态加载内容，自动提取标题和正文并保存为 Markdown 文件。本技能应在用户需要抓取微信公众号文章内容时使用。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/wechat-article-fetch/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>wechat-article-search</name>\n      <description>当用户明确要求搜索微信公众号文章、公众号推文、某个公众号最近文章，或按关键词查找微信公众号文章时使用本技能。本技能通过搜狗微信搜索返回结构化文章信息，包括标题、摘要、发布时间、来源公众号和链接。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/wechat-article-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"cc6ee8b6-0420-4f81-b1da-560f58730fdd"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：政策法规。场景ID：policy_regulation\n识别场景：政策法规 (policy_regulation)；场景模式：single；候选场景：policy_regulation\n任务切分：\n- 请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。\n任务规划：\n1. 检索与解析禁停区管理规范：基于政策法规场景能力，定向检索地方性交通管理条例及交管部门关于“禁止停车区域”的认定标准与违停时间界定条款；提取核心合规依据（如连续停放阈值、临时停靠豁免条件）；输出结构化政策条文清单及关键时间参数。\n2. 构建连续性判定逻辑模型：结合目标轨迹监测特征与已提取的政策时间阈值，规划从单帧检测到时序连续性的转换规则；明确关键指标（如有效停留时长计算口径、跨帧去重机制、中断判定容差）；输出目标连续驻留的时间序列处理方案。\n3. 映射合规要求与技术判别标准：将法规中的“连续5分钟”定义与轨迹数据的时间戳连续性要求进行对齐分析；设定阶段性产出为合规判定对照表，明确满足连续违规的技术条件与排除单帧误报的过滤策略。\n4. 生成标准化合规研判流程：整合政策依据与轨迹分析逻辑，制定可执行的判定时序步骤；明确输入数据格式要求、中间校验节点及最终输出格式（合规/疑似违规/证据不足）；形成面向后续智能体调用的标准化判定SOP文档。\n场景任务：\n- policy_regulation: 我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。；参数：{'政策主题': '禁停区停车时长规定', '分析目标': '合规判断'}\n已提取参数：{'政策主题': '禁停区停车时长规定', '分析目标': '合规判断'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：政策主题。需要查询、解读、对比或引用的政策法规主题\n- 提取可选参数：地区或层级。政策法规适用的地区、行政层级、行业领域或发布主体\n- 提取可选参数：分析目标。用户需要执行的动作，如查询条文、解释政策、合规判断、生成依据、对比差异、合同审查、法律咨询、诉讼分析、专利分析、商标申请、法律文书、公文写作等\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d5e64d4b-06ce-449c-b936-0c62f3531f08"},{"content":"判断目标是否**连续**5分钟出现在禁停区，核心在于从\"单帧检测\"升级为\"跨帧时序追踪\"。下面给出完整方案：\n\n---\n\n## 一、判定逻辑框架\n\n| 判定维度 | 关键要点 |\n|---------|---------|\n| **时间连续性** | 目标ID在相邻帧之间不断裂（同一目标不被误拆或误合并） |\n| **空间一致性** | 目标始终位于禁停区的地理围栏内 |\n| **有效停留时长** | 累计 ≥ 300秒（可设容差 ±N 秒） |\n| **中断判定** | 目标消失超过容差阈值后重新出现 → 视为中断，时间重置 |\n\n---\n\n## 二、具体实施步骤\n\n### 第1步：获取带时间戳的轨迹数据\n\n通过视频分析工具对禁停区域进行持续检测/追踪，输出每帧中目标的：\n\n- **唯一目标ID**（track ID）\n- **中心坐标**（判断是否在禁停区内）\n- **时间戳**（精确到秒）\n- **置信度**（过滤低质量检测）\n\n### 第2步：计算连续停留时长\n\n```\n伪代码逻辑：\n1. 按目标ID分组所有检测记录\n2. 对每个目标ID的记录按时间戳排序\n3. 遍历记录，检查相邻帧的时间间隔 Δt：\n   - 如果 Δt ≤ 容差阈值（如 3~5 秒）→ 属于同一段连续停留\n   - 如果 Δt > 容差阈值 → 前一段结束，新的一段开始\n4. 累加每段的有效停留总时长\n5. 如果任一段 ≥ 300秒 → 判定为\"连续5分钟违规\"\n```\n\n### 第3步：容差设计\n\n为避免短暂信号丢失导致误判，建议设置：\n\n- **最大允许中断时间**：3~5秒（即目标短暂被遮挡后恢复仍可算作连续）\n- **最低检测频率**：至少每秒1帧以上\n- **置信度下限**：剔除置信度过低的误检\n\n---\n\n## 三、技术实现方式\n\n如果你有**视频文件**，我可以直接使用视频分析工具进行检测和追踪：\n\n> **需要提供：** 视频文件路径\n\n如果你有**已检测出的结构化数据**（CSV/Excel），我也可以帮你做时序分析：\n\n> **需要提供：** 包含目标ID、时间戳、坐标的数据文件\n\n---\n\n## 四、输出结果格式\n\n最终输出类似：\n\n```\n目标ID: TRACK_007\n首次出现: 2026-07-23 10:15:22\n末次出现: 2026-07-23 10:21:48\n中间是否有中断: 否（最大空档 2秒）\n连续停留时长: 386秒\n判定结论: ✅ 连续5分钟出现在禁停区（违规）\n```\n\n---\n\n**请告诉我你目前有什么类型的数据？** 是视频文件、检测结果的CSV/Excel，还是其他格式？我会根据实际数据给出具体的分析操作。","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":934,"prompt_tokens":13132,"total_tokens":14066,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":234,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":934},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13132}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-2263e145-85e9-9633-ad64-45492bf75d4b","finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f79-67d6-77b0-9136-66a9b8bd2b76-0","tool_calls":[],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13132,"output_tokens":934,"total_tokens":14066,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":234}}}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/cd6db180-431d-4187-86a7-114643690ae8/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/cd6db180-431d-4187-86a7-114643690ae8/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/cd6db180-431d-4187-86a7-114643690ae8/user-data/outputs"},"title":"禁停区连续停留判定","artifacts":[],"raw_messages":[{"content":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"d7d8f4ef-6fb1-449d-95f4-d11cfedf7409"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-contract-review</name>\n      <description>中国合同审查 skill。\nUse this skill when the user provides a full contract text, a draft agreement,\nor concrete clauses and wants structured review on:\n- contract validity\n- rights and obligations\n- breach / default clauses\n- risk points\n- revision suggestions\n- dispute resolution clause risks\nDo NOT use this skill for full dispute analysis driven by case facts.\nIf the task is to analyze a dispute, identify claims/defenses, or build evidence strategy,\nuse china-legal-issue-analysis instead.\nIf the user only needs a lightweight initial consultation without clause-level review,\nuse china-legal-consultation.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-contract-review/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-legal-consultation</name>\n      <description>中国法律咨询 skill。\nUse this skill when a party describes a legal problem and mainly wants:\n- legal relationship explanation\n- risk reminders\n- rights-protection path guidance\n- evidence suggestions\n- practical notes / cautions\nDo NOT use this skill for full contract redlining or the full dispute-analysis path.\nIf the user needs full case analysis, use china-legal-issue-analysis.\nIf the user provides a full contract for clause review, use china-contract-review.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-legal-consultation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-legal-issue-analysis</name>\n      <description>中国法律问题分析 skill。\nUse this skill for concrete Chinese legal issues, dispute analysis,\nissue spotting, legal relationship analysis, risk assessment,\nlitigation/arbitration positioning, and action planning.\nCore capabilities:\n- case type identification\n- six-part checklist generation\n- 10-step legal analysis process\n- IRAC / claim-right / issue-based analysis\n- domain-specific issue analysis\n- legal citation verification and revision\nDo NOT use this skill as a dedicated contract redlining skill.\nIf the primary input is a full contract text that needs clause-by-clause review,\nuse china-contract-review instead.\nIf the user only needs a lightweight initial answer as a party to a dispute,\nuse china-legal-consultation instead.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-legal-issue-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>chinese-policy-analysis</name>\n      <description>This skill should be used when the user asks to \"分析中国政策\", \"评估政策落地可能性\", \"判断政策执行力度\", \"预判政策走向\", \"解读政策文件\", or needs systematic framework to analyze Chinese government policy implementation likelihood, execution paths, and actual impact.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/chinese-policy-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code2patent</name>\n      <description>从已开发代码项目中提取技术实现证据，围绕候选专利方案生成技术交底书，并以“权利要求布局卡 → 发明专利初稿”两步法继续生成接近可申报版的中国发明专利起草材料。触发场景包括：读取代码仓库后撰写技术交底书、将人工总结的专利方案映射到具体实现、从代码中挖掘可专利技术方案、为专利代理师准备权利要求布局和发明专利初稿。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/code2patent/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>law-local-retrieval</name>\n      <description>基于 Elasticsearch 的政策法规条文检索 Skill。适用于从已建立的政策法规 ES 索引中检索中国法律法规、政策文件、法律条文、政策依据、执法依据、效力状态、发布机关、发布日期、实施日期等信息，并为政策分析报告、合规审查、执法风险分析提供可回溯的法规依据。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/law-local-retrieval/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-briefing</name>\n      <description>中国法律材料整理、备忘录撰写与报告生成助手。\nThis skill is NOT the primary legal retrieval skill.\nUse it only after legal materials have already been retrieved, analyzed, or explicitly provided by the user.\nCore responsibilities:\n- organize already retrieved statutes, judicial interpretations, cases, and policy materials\n- turn existing legal materials into structured briefings, memos, summaries, and risk notes\n- compare multiple rules and explain their relationship in a concise, usable format\n- adapt output depth and style for different user roles\nDo NOT use this skill as the first-step legal retrieval skill for:\n- 查法条原文\n- 查第几条怎么规定\n- 查司法解释/法规/规范性文件\n- 询问“法律依据是什么”\n- 询问“根据什么法律”</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-briefing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-document-assistant</name>\n      <description>提供常见法律文书模板与撰写指导，涵盖劳务纠纷、离婚协议、交通事故、租房协议等场景；当用户需要法律文书模板、撰写建议或遇到法律纠纷时使用</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-document-assistant/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-proposal-generator</name>\n      <description>根据案件材料或沟通记录生成各类法律服务文档（诉讼方案、咨询报告、非诉方案、建议书、沟通报告、案件分析摘要等）。本技能应在用户需要将案件材料、咨询记录或沟通内容整理为专业法律文档时使用。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-proposal-generator/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-qa-extractor</name>\n      <description>从律师与客户沟通记录中提取有价值的法律问答对，生成结构化知识库内容。本技能应在用户需要整理客户咨询记录、从对话中提取可复用法律知识、创建问答知识库、或准备内容营销素材时使用。支持严格客户信息脱敏处理。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-qa-extractor/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-text-format</name>\n      <description>将法律文本（法律条文或法律案例）转换为规范的 Markdown 格式，删除推广冗余信息。本技能应在用户需要处理法律条文（如民法典、刑法等）、整理法律案例（如最高法典型案例、裁判文书等）、或从粘贴文本中格式化法律文档时使用。注意：本技能只负责格式化和内容清理，不包含内容抓取能力。内容获取应由其他 skill（如 wechat-article-fetch）完成，AI 会自动判断技能协作顺序。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-text-format/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>litigation-analysis</name>\n      <description>诉讼分析工具 - 判决书深度分析，生成上诉/再审决策支持</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/litigation-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>official-document-writer</name>\n      <description>Use this skill only when the user explicitly asks to draft, polish, revise, or export a formal Chinese official document such as 请示、报告、汇报材料、公文草拟. The skill should first gather authoritative policy basis from available web search/fetch tools or user-provided/local materials, then draft the document in formal official Chinese style. Do not use this skill for general policy Q&A, legal retrieval, ordinary article writing, or broad research tasks.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/official-document-writer/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>patent-analysis</name>\n      <description>当需要分析专利文件、进行侵权评估、提取技术特征、或比较多个专利的保护范围时使用。触发场景包括专利比对、权利要求分析、侵权检查、专利技术要点总结、专利稳定性分析、专利价值评估、FTO分析。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/patent-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>policy-rag</name>\n      <description>当用户需要处理企业内部制度文件、审批流程表、审批权责表，或需要基于内部制度与审批流进行检索、问答、索引构建时，使用本技能。适用于制度文档拆分、Excel 审批表转换、制度索引构建、制度条款检索、审批路径检索等场景。不适用于国家法律法规、司法解释、裁判案例等法律检索任务；此类问题应交由专门的法律检索技能处理。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/policy-rag/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>trademark-assistant</name>\n      <description>面向中国商标申请的类别规划、可注册性初筛及申请材料准备技能。基于尼斯分类（国际商标分类），引用中国法律法规。本技能应在接到商标咨询、需要结构化输出建议与风险分级、或需要准备申请材料时使用。不要用于：替代正式法律意见、承诺注册成功率、处理复杂商标争议案件。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/trademark-assistant/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>wechat-article-fetch</name>\n      <description>抓取微信公众号文章内容，使用 Playwright headless 模式无弹窗后台抓取，支持动态加载内容，自动提取标题和正文并保存为 Markdown 文件。本技能应在用户需要抓取微信公众号文章内容时使用。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/wechat-article-fetch/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>wechat-article-search</name>\n      <description>当用户明确要求搜索微信公众号文章、公众号推文、某个公众号最近文章，或按关键词查找微信公众号文章时使用本技能。本技能通过搜狗微信搜索返回结构化文章信息，包括标题、摘要、发布时间、来源公众号和链接。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/wechat-article-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"cc6ee8b6-0420-4f81-b1da-560f58730fdd"}],"viewed_images":{},"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","normalized_query":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","routing_query":"场景：政策法规。场景ID：policy_regulation。场景说明：政策、法规、制度、条例、通知、合规依据、法律条文查询与解读，以及中国法律咨询、合同审查、诉讼分析、专利商标、法律文书、公文写作、微信公众号法律文章检索和企业内部制度检索场景。需要识别参数：政策主题、地区或层级、分析目标。用户原始问题：我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现","scene":"policy_regulation","scene_name":"政策法规","params":{"政策主题":"禁停区停车时长规定","分析目标":"合规判断"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["policy_regulation"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_78924c","text":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_4c821c","text":"检索与解析禁停区管理规范：基于政策法规场景能力，定向检索地方性交通管理条例及交管部门关于“禁止停车区域”的认定标准与违停时间界定条款；提取核心合规依据（如连续停放阈值、临时停靠豁免条件）；输出结构化政策条文清单及关键时间参数。"},{"task_span_id":"span_e47f29","text":"构建连续性判定逻辑模型：结合目标轨迹监测特征与已提取的政策时间阈值，规划从单帧检测到时序连续性的转换规则；明确关键指标（如有效停留时长计算口径、跨帧去重机制、中断判定容差）；输出目标连续驻留的时间序列处理方案。"},{"task_span_id":"span_095ad5","text":"映射合规要求与技术判别标准：将法规中的“连续5分钟”定义与轨迹数据的时间戳连续性要求进行对齐分析；设定阶段性产出为合规判定对照表，明确满足连续违规的技术条件与排除单帧误报的过滤策略。"},{"task_span_id":"span_26c0db","text":"生成标准化合规研判流程：整合政策依据与轨迹分析逻辑，制定可执行的判定时序步骤；明确输入数据格式要求、中间校验节点及最终输出格式（合规/疑似违规/证据不足）；形成面向后续智能体调用的标准化判定SOP文档。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_258f29","scene":"policy_regulation","scene_name":"政策法规","text":"我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","params":{"政策主题":"禁停区停车时长规定","分析目标":"合规判断"}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_258f29","scene":"policy_regulation","scene_name":"政策法规","text":"我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","params":{"政策主题":"禁停区停车时长规定","分析目标":"合规判断"}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：政策主题。需要查询、解读、对比或引用的政策法规主题","提取可选参数：地区或层级。政策法规适用的地区、行政层级、行业领域或发布主体","提取可选参数：分析目标。用户需要执行的动作，如查询条文、解释政策、合规判断、生成依据、对比差异、合同审查、法律咨询、诉讼分析、专利分析、商标申请、法律文书、公文写作等"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:d7d8f4ef-6fb1-449d-95f4-d11cfedf7409"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":true,"primary_goal":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","scene":"policy_regulation","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[{"id":"china-contract-review","role":"primary","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"china-legal-consultation","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"china-legal-issue-analysis","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"chinese-policy-analysis","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"code2patent","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"law-local-retrieval","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"legal-briefing","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"legal-document-assistant","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"legal-proposal-generator","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"legal-qa-extractor","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"legal-text-format","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"litigation-analysis","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"official-document-writer","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"patent-analysis","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"policy-rag","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"trademark-assistant","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"wechat-article-fetch","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null},{"id":"wechat-article-search","role":"supporting","score":1.0,"reason":null}],"expected_outputs":[],"depends_on":[]}],"global_selected_skills":["china-contract-review","china-legal-consultation","china-legal-issue-analysis","chinese-policy-analysis","code2patent","law-local-retrieval","legal-briefing","legal-document-assistant","legal-proposal-generator","legal-qa-extractor","legal-text-format","litigation-analysis","official-document-writer","patent-analysis","policy-rag","trademark-assistant","wechat-article-fetch","wechat-article-search"],"default_public_skill_ids":[],"global_allowed_tools":[],"confidence":1.0,"route_reason":"SkillRouter disabled; injected all custom skills for detected intent scene as LeadAgent candidate skills","allowed_skills":["china-contract-review","china-legal-consultation","china-legal-issue-analysis","chinese-policy-analysis","code2patent","law-local-retrieval","legal-briefing","legal-document-assistant","legal-proposal-generator","legal-qa-extractor","legal-text-format","litigation-analysis","official-document-writer","patent-analysis","policy-rag","trademark-assistant","wechat-article-fetch","wechat-article-search"],"selection_owner":"lead_agent","_source_message_key":"id:d7d8f4ef-6fb1-449d-95f4-d11cfedf7409"},"dialogue_context":{"act":"new_task","confidence":0.7,"reason":"no_pending_action_match","parsed_answer":null,"pending_action_id":null,"resume_intent_context":null,"resume_routing_context":null,"metadata":{}},"final_scope_skill_ids":["china-contract-review","china-legal-consultation","china-legal-issue-analysis","chinese-policy-analysis","code2patent","law-local-retrieval","legal-briefing","legal-document-assistant","legal-proposal-generator","legal-qa-extractor","legal-text-format","litigation-analysis","official-document-writer","patent-analysis","policy-rag","trademark-assistant","wechat-article-fetch","wechat-article-search"],"allowed_tool_names":[]}

event: values
data: {"messages":[{"content":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"d7d8f4ef-6fb1-449d-95f4-d11cfedf7409"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-contract-review</name>\n      <description>中国合同审查 skill。\nUse this skill when the user provides a full contract text, a draft agreement,\nor concrete clauses and wants structured review on:\n- contract validity\n- rights and obligations\n- breach / default clauses\n- risk points\n- revision suggestions\n- dispute resolution clause risks\nDo NOT use this skill for full dispute analysis driven by case facts.\nIf the task is to analyze a dispute, identify claims/defenses, or build evidence strategy,\nuse china-legal-issue-analysis instead.\nIf the user only needs a lightweight initial consultation without clause-level review,\nuse china-legal-consultation.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-contract-review/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-legal-consultation</name>\n      <description>中国法律咨询 skill。\nUse this skill when a party describes a legal problem and mainly wants:\n- legal relationship explanation\n- risk reminders\n- rights-protection path guidance\n- evidence suggestions\n- practical notes / cautions\nDo NOT use this skill for full contract redlining or the full dispute-analysis path.\nIf the user needs full case analysis, use china-legal-issue-analysis.\nIf the user provides a full contract for clause review, use china-contract-review.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-legal-consultation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-legal-issue-analysis</name>\n      <description>中国法律问题分析 skill。\nUse this skill for concrete Chinese legal issues, dispute analysis,\nissue spotting, legal relationship analysis, risk assessment,\nlitigation/arbitration positioning, and action planning.\nCore capabilities:\n- case type identification\n- six-part checklist generation\n- 10-step legal analysis process\n- IRAC / claim-right / issue-based analysis\n- domain-specific issue analysis\n- legal citation verification and revision\nDo NOT use this skill as a dedicated contract redlining skill.\nIf the primary input is a full contract text that needs clause-by-clause review,\nuse china-contract-review instead.\nIf the user only needs a lightweight initial answer as a party to a dispute,\nuse china-legal-consultation instead.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-legal-issue-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>chinese-policy-analysis</name>\n      <description>This skill should be used when the user asks to \"分析中国政策\", \"评估政策落地可能性\", \"判断政策执行力度\", \"预判政策走向\", \"解读政策文件\", or needs systematic framework to analyze Chinese government policy implementation likelihood, execution paths, and actual impact.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/chinese-policy-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code2patent</name>\n      <description>从已开发代码项目中提取技术实现证据，围绕候选专利方案生成技术交底书，并以“权利要求布局卡 → 发明专利初稿”两步法继续生成接近可申报版的中国发明专利起草材料。触发场景包括：读取代码仓库后撰写技术交底书、将人工总结的专利方案映射到具体实现、从代码中挖掘可专利技术方案、为专利代理师准备权利要求布局和发明专利初稿。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/code2patent/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>law-local-retrieval</name>\n      <description>基于 Elasticsearch 的政策法规条文检索 Skill。适用于从已建立的政策法规 ES 索引中检索中国法律法规、政策文件、法律条文、政策依据、执法依据、效力状态、发布机关、发布日期、实施日期等信息，并为政策分析报告、合规审查、执法风险分析提供可回溯的法规依据。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/law-local-retrieval/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-briefing</name>\n      <description>中国法律材料整理、备忘录撰写与报告生成助手。\nThis skill is NOT the primary legal retrieval skill.\nUse it only after legal materials have already been retrieved, analyzed, or explicitly provided by the user.\nCore responsibilities:\n- organize already retrieved statutes, judicial interpretations, cases, and policy materials\n- turn existing legal materials into structured briefings, memos, summaries, and risk notes\n- compare multiple rules and explain their relationship in a concise, usable format\n- adapt output depth and style for different user roles\nDo NOT use this skill as the first-step legal retrieval skill for:\n- 查法条原文\n- 查第几条怎么规定\n- 查司法解释/法规/规范性文件\n- 询问“法律依据是什么”\n- 询问“根据什么法律”</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-briefing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-document-assistant</name>\n      <description>提供常见法律文书模板与撰写指导，涵盖劳务纠纷、离婚协议、交通事故、租房协议等场景；当用户需要法律文书模板、撰写建议或遇到法律纠纷时使用</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-document-assistant/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-proposal-generator</name>\n      <description>根据案件材料或沟通记录生成各类法律服务文档（诉讼方案、咨询报告、非诉方案、建议书、沟通报告、案件分析摘要等）。本技能应在用户需要将案件材料、咨询记录或沟通内容整理为专业法律文档时使用。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-proposal-generator/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-qa-extractor</name>\n      <description>从律师与客户沟通记录中提取有价值的法律问答对，生成结构化知识库内容。本技能应在用户需要整理客户咨询记录、从对话中提取可复用法律知识、创建问答知识库、或准备内容营销素材时使用。支持严格客户信息脱敏处理。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-qa-extractor/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-text-format</name>\n      <description>将法律文本（法律条文或法律案例）转换为规范的 Markdown 格式，删除推广冗余信息。本技能应在用户需要处理法律条文（如民法典、刑法等）、整理法律案例（如最高法典型案例、裁判文书等）、或从粘贴文本中格式化法律文档时使用。注意：本技能只负责格式化和内容清理，不包含内容抓取能力。内容获取应由其他 skill（如 wechat-article-fetch）完成，AI 会自动判断技能协作顺序。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-text-format/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>litigation-analysis</name>\n      <description>诉讼分析工具 - 判决书深度分析，生成上诉/再审决策支持</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/litigation-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>official-document-writer</name>\n      <description>Use this skill only when the user explicitly asks to draft, polish, revise, or export a formal Chinese official document such as 请示、报告、汇报材料、公文草拟. The skill should first gather authoritative policy basis from available web search/fetch tools or user-provided/local materials, then draft the document in formal official Chinese style. Do not use this skill for general policy Q&A, legal retrieval, ordinary article writing, or broad research tasks.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/official-document-writer/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>patent-analysis</name>\n      <description>当需要分析专利文件、进行侵权评估、提取技术特征、或比较多个专利的保护范围时使用。触发场景包括专利比对、权利要求分析、侵权检查、专利技术要点总结、专利稳定性分析、专利价值评估、FTO分析。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/patent-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>policy-rag</name>\n      <description>当用户需要处理企业内部制度文件、审批流程表、审批权责表，或需要基于内部制度与审批流进行检索、问答、索引构建时，使用本技能。适用于制度文档拆分、Excel 审批表转换、制度索引构建、制度条款检索、审批路径检索等场景。不适用于国家法律法规、司法解释、裁判案例等法律检索任务；此类问题应交由专门的法律检索技能处理。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/policy-rag/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>trademark-assistant</name>\n      <description>面向中国商标申请的类别规划、可注册性初筛及申请材料准备技能。基于尼斯分类（国际商标分类），引用中国法律法规。本技能应在接到商标咨询、需要结构化输出建议与风险分级、或需要准备申请材料时使用。不要用于：替代正式法律意见、承诺注册成功率、处理复杂商标争议案件。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/trademark-assistant/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>wechat-article-fetch</name>\n      <description>抓取微信公众号文章内容，使用 Playwright headless 模式无弹窗后台抓取，支持动态加载内容，自动提取标题和正文并保存为 Markdown 文件。本技能应在用户需要抓取微信公众号文章内容时使用。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/wechat-article-fetch/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>wechat-article-search</name>\n      <description>当用户明确要求搜索微信公众号文章、公众号推文、某个公众号最近文章，或按关键词查找微信公众号文章时使用本技能。本技能通过搜狗微信搜索返回结构化文章信息，包括标题、摘要、发布时间、来源公众号和链接。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/wechat-article-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"cc6ee8b6-0420-4f81-b1da-560f58730fdd"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：政策法规。场景ID：policy_regulation\n识别场景：政策法规 (policy_regulation)；场景模式：single；候选场景：policy_regulation\n任务切分：\n- 请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。\n任务规划：\n1. 检索与解析禁停区管理规范：基于政策法规场景能力，定向检索地方性交通管理条例及交管部门关于“禁止停车区域”的认定标准与违停时间界定条款；提取核心合规依据（如连续停放阈值、临时停靠豁免条件）；输出结构化政策条文清单及关键时间参数。\n2. 构建连续性判定逻辑模型：结合目标轨迹监测特征与已提取的政策时间阈值，规划从单帧检测到时序连续性的转换规则；明确关键指标（如有效停留时长计算口径、跨帧去重机制、中断判定容差）；输出目标连续驻留的时间序列处理方案。\n3. 映射合规要求与技术判别标准：将法规中的“连续5分钟”定义与轨迹数据的时间戳连续性要求进行对齐分析；设定阶段性产出为合规判定对照表，明确满足连续违规的技术条件与排除单帧误报的过滤策略。\n4. 生成标准化合规研判流程：整合政策依据与轨迹分析逻辑，制定可执行的判定时序步骤；明确输入数据格式要求、中间校验节点及最终输出格式（合规/疑似违规/证据不足）；形成面向后续智能体调用的标准化判定SOP文档。\n场景任务：\n- policy_regulation: 我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。；参数：{'政策主题': '禁停区停车时长规定', '分析目标': '合规判断'}\n已提取参数：{'政策主题': '禁停区停车时长规定', '分析目标': '合规判断'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：政策主题。需要查询、解读、对比或引用的政策法规主题\n- 提取可选参数：地区或层级。政策法规适用的地区、行政层级、行业领域或发布主体\n- 提取可选参数：分析目标。用户需要执行的动作，如查询条文、解释政策、合规判断、生成依据、对比差异、合同审查、法律咨询、诉讼分析、专利分析、商标申请、法律文书、公文写作等\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d5e64d4b-06ce-449c-b936-0c62f3531f08"},{"content":"判断目标是否**连续**5分钟出现在禁停区，核心在于从\"单帧检测\"升级为\"跨帧时序追踪\"。下面给出完整方案：\n\n---\n\n## 一、判定逻辑框架\n\n| 判定维度 | 关键要点 |\n|---------|---------|\n| **时间连续性** | 目标ID在相邻帧之间不断裂（同一目标不被误拆或误合并） |\n| **空间一致性** | 目标始终位于禁停区的地理围栏内 |\n| **有效停留时长** | 累计 ≥ 300秒（可设容差 ±N 秒） |\n| **中断判定** | 目标消失超过容差阈值后重新出现 → 视为中断，时间重置 |\n\n---\n\n## 二、具体实施步骤\n\n### 第1步：获取带时间戳的轨迹数据\n\n通过视频分析工具对禁停区域进行持续检测/追踪，输出每帧中目标的：\n\n- **唯一目标ID**（track ID）\n- **中心坐标**（判断是否在禁停区内）\n- **时间戳**（精确到秒）\n- **置信度**（过滤低质量检测）\n\n### 第2步：计算连续停留时长\n\n```\n伪代码逻辑：\n1. 按目标ID分组所有检测记录\n2. 对每个目标ID的记录按时间戳排序\n3. 遍历记录，检查相邻帧的时间间隔 Δt：\n   - 如果 Δt ≤ 容差阈值（如 3~5 秒）→ 属于同一段连续停留\n   - 如果 Δt > 容差阈值 → 前一段结束，新的一段开始\n4. 累加每段的有效停留总时长\n5. 如果任一段 ≥ 300秒 → 判定为\"连续5分钟违规\"\n```\n\n### 第3步：容差设计\n\n为避免短暂信号丢失导致误判，建议设置：\n\n- **最大允许中断时间**：3~5秒（即目标短暂被遮挡后恢复仍可算作连续）\n- **最低检测频率**：至少每秒1帧以上\n- **置信度下限**：剔除置信度过低的误检\n\n---\n\n## 三、技术实现方式\n\n如果你有**视频文件**，我可以直接使用视频分析工具进行检测和追踪：\n\n> **需要提供：** 视频文件路径\n\n如果你有**已检测出的结构化数据**（CSV/Excel），我也可以帮你做时序分析：\n\n> **需要提供：** 包含目标ID、时间戳、坐标的数据文件\n\n---\n\n## 四、输出结果格式\n\n最终输出类似：\n\n```\n目标ID: TRACK_007\n首次出现: 2026-07-23 10:15:22\n末次出现: 2026-07-23 10:21:48\n中间是否有中断: 否（最大空档 2秒）\n连续停留时长: 386秒\n判定结论: ✅ 连续5分钟出现在禁停区（违规）\n```\n\n---\n\n**请告诉我你目前有什么类型的数据？** 是视频文件、检测结果的CSV/Excel，还是其他格式？我会根据实际数据给出具体的分析操作。","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":934,"prompt_tokens":13132,"total_tokens":14066,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":234,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":934},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13132}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-2263e145-85e9-9633-ad64-45492bf75d4b","finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f79-67d6-77b0-9136-66a9b8bd2b76-0","tool_calls":[],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13132,"output_tokens":934,"total_tokens":14066,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":234}}}],"thread_data":{"workspace_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/cd6db180-431d-4187-86a7-114643690ae8/user-data/workspace","uploads_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/cd6db180-431d-4187-86a7-114643690ae8/user-data/uploads","outputs_path":"/app/backend/.deer-flow/threads/cd6db180-431d-4187-86a7-114643690ae8/user-data/outputs"},"title":"禁停区连续停留判定","artifacts":[],"raw_messages":[{"content":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":null,"id":"d7d8f4ef-6fb1-449d-95f4-d11cfedf7409"},{"content":"<skill_system source=\"skill_router\">\nYou have access to skills that provide optimized workflows for specific tasks. Each skill contains best practices, frameworks, and references to additional resources.\n\n**Skill Availability Rules:**\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt are available across turns.\n- Custom/domain skills are available only when listed in a current-turn routed <available_skills> section.\n- Ignore custom/domain skills mentioned in previous turns if they are not listed in the current turn.\n- Do not call tools associated with unavailable skills.\n- If a later current-turn routed_skill_prompt is injected by SkillRouter, its <available_skills> list recommends the custom/domain skills for this turn; public skills from the base prompt remain available as supporting workflows.\n- When SkillRouter ranking is disabled and scene filtering injects all skills for a scene, treat <available_skills> as an allowed candidate set. Select the specific skill or skills that match the current user request before loading skill files or executing workflows.\n\n**Override Scope:**\n- This routed <skill_system> lists recommended custom/domain skills for the current turn.\n- It does NOT replace the base system prompt.\n- Public skills listed in the base system prompt remain available for supporting operations.\n- When uploaded structured files (Excel, CSV, JSON, Parquet, or similar tabular evidence) are central to the user's request, use the public data-analysis skill first to inspect and extract facts before domain synthesis.\n- Continue following language_policy, clarification_system, working_directory, response_style, and critical_reminders from the base system prompt.\n\n**Progressive Loading Pattern:**\n1. When a user query matches an available skill's use case, first choose the concrete skill.\n2. Call `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode for that selected skill to create and validate the SkillInputEnvelope and legacy invocation package.\n3. Read the returned skill file path and understand the skill's workflow and instructions.\n4. The skill file contains references to external resources under the same folder.\n5. Load referenced resources only when needed during execution.\n6. Follow the skill's instructions precisely.\n7. After legacy execution, call `invoke_skill` in `wrap_output` mode to normalize the result into SkillResult when a machine-readable Skill output is needed.\n\n**Mandatory Skill Execution Discipline:**\n- Calling `invoke_skill` in `prepare` mode is NOT sufficient. It only prepares the selected Skill invocation. After `prepare`, you MUST actually execute the selected Skill workflow.\n- After `invoke_skill(mode=\"prepare\")` returns `legacy_invocation.container_skill_file`, you MUST read that Skill file and treat it as the authoritative execution guide.\n- If the Skill provides scripts, commands, templates, references, or executable workflows, you MUST use those Skill-provided assets first.\n- Do NOT replace a matched Skill workflow with ad hoc Python, pandas, SQL, shell, or manual analysis code before attempting the Skill workflow.\n- For `data-analysis`, if `/mnt/skills/public/data-analysis/scripts/analyze.py` is available and the task is structured data analysis, you MUST call that script first for data inspection, SQL query, aggregation, statistics, or chart preparation. Do not write standalone pandas code for the same operation before trying this script.\n- Custom code is allowed only after one of these conditions is true:\n  1. the selected Skill file does not provide a suitable executable workflow;\n  2. the Skill-provided script or workflow has been attempted and failed;\n  3. the user explicitly requests custom code;\n  4. the required operation is clearly outside the Skill's documented capability.\n- When you fall back to custom code, briefly state that the Skill workflow was insufficient or failed, and continue from the Skill result or error.\n\n**Skill Loading Priority Rules:**\n- If a request clearly matches an available skill and also includes uploaded files, load the skill file before reading uploaded data files.\n- Do NOT read a full uploaded structured data file before loading the matched skill.\n- For uploaded structured data files, use small previews only when needed.\n- Prefer the matched skill's scripts, workflows, or tools for actual analysis.\n- Do not start by generating ad hoc JS, Python, SQL, or shell scripts when a matched skill exists.\n- Only improvise custom code after loading the matched skill and confirming the skill does not already provide a suitable workflow.\n\n**Skills are located at:** /mnt/skills\n\n<available_skills>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-contract-review</name>\n      <description>中国合同审查 skill。\nUse this skill when the user provides a full contract text, a draft agreement,\nor concrete clauses and wants structured review on:\n- contract validity\n- rights and obligations\n- breach / default clauses\n- risk points\n- revision suggestions\n- dispute resolution clause risks\nDo NOT use this skill for full dispute analysis driven by case facts.\nIf the task is to analyze a dispute, identify claims/defenses, or build evidence strategy,\nuse china-legal-issue-analysis instead.\nIf the user only needs a lightweight initial consultation without clause-level review,\nuse china-legal-consultation.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-contract-review/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-legal-consultation</name>\n      <description>中国法律咨询 skill。\nUse this skill when a party describes a legal problem and mainly wants:\n- legal relationship explanation\n- risk reminders\n- rights-protection path guidance\n- evidence suggestions\n- practical notes / cautions\nDo NOT use this skill for full contract redlining or the full dispute-analysis path.\nIf the user needs full case analysis, use china-legal-issue-analysis.\nIf the user provides a full contract for clause review, use china-contract-review.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-legal-consultation/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>china-legal-issue-analysis</name>\n      <description>中国法律问题分析 skill。\nUse this skill for concrete Chinese legal issues, dispute analysis,\nissue spotting, legal relationship analysis, risk assessment,\nlitigation/arbitration positioning, and action planning.\nCore capabilities:\n- case type identification\n- six-part checklist generation\n- 10-step legal analysis process\n- IRAC / claim-right / issue-based analysis\n- domain-specific issue analysis\n- legal citation verification and revision\nDo NOT use this skill as a dedicated contract redlining skill.\nIf the primary input is a full contract text that needs clause-by-clause review,\nuse china-contract-review instead.\nIf the user only needs a lightweight initial answer as a party to a dispute,\nuse china-legal-consultation instead.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/china-legal-issue-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>chinese-policy-analysis</name>\n      <description>This skill should be used when the user asks to \"分析中国政策\", \"评估政策落地可能性\", \"判断政策执行力度\", \"预判政策走向\", \"解读政策文件\", or needs systematic framework to analyze Chinese government policy implementation likelihood, execution paths, and actual impact.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/chinese-policy-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>code2patent</name>\n      <description>从已开发代码项目中提取技术实现证据，围绕候选专利方案生成技术交底书，并以“权利要求布局卡 → 发明专利初稿”两步法继续生成接近可申报版的中国发明专利起草材料。触发场景包括：读取代码仓库后撰写技术交底书、将人工总结的专利方案映射到具体实现、从代码中挖掘可专利技术方案、为专利代理师准备权利要求布局和发明专利初稿。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/code2patent/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>law-local-retrieval</name>\n      <description>基于 Elasticsearch 的政策法规条文检索 Skill。适用于从已建立的政策法规 ES 索引中检索中国法律法规、政策文件、法律条文、政策依据、执法依据、效力状态、发布机关、发布日期、实施日期等信息，并为政策分析报告、合规审查、执法风险分析提供可回溯的法规依据。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/law-local-retrieval/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-briefing</name>\n      <description>中国法律材料整理、备忘录撰写与报告生成助手。\nThis skill is NOT the primary legal retrieval skill.\nUse it only after legal materials have already been retrieved, analyzed, or explicitly provided by the user.\nCore responsibilities:\n- organize already retrieved statutes, judicial interpretations, cases, and policy materials\n- turn existing legal materials into structured briefings, memos, summaries, and risk notes\n- compare multiple rules and explain their relationship in a concise, usable format\n- adapt output depth and style for different user roles\nDo NOT use this skill as the first-step legal retrieval skill for:\n- 查法条原文\n- 查第几条怎么规定\n- 查司法解释/法规/规范性文件\n- 询问“法律依据是什么”\n- 询问“根据什么法律”</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-briefing/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-document-assistant</name>\n      <description>提供常见法律文书模板与撰写指导，涵盖劳务纠纷、离婚协议、交通事故、租房协议等场景；当用户需要法律文书模板、撰写建议或遇到法律纠纷时使用</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-document-assistant/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-proposal-generator</name>\n      <description>根据案件材料或沟通记录生成各类法律服务文档（诉讼方案、咨询报告、非诉方案、建议书、沟通报告、案件分析摘要等）。本技能应在用户需要将案件材料、咨询记录或沟通内容整理为专业法律文档时使用。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-proposal-generator/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-qa-extractor</name>\n      <description>从律师与客户沟通记录中提取有价值的法律问答对，生成结构化知识库内容。本技能应在用户需要整理客户咨询记录、从对话中提取可复用法律知识、创建问答知识库、或准备内容营销素材时使用。支持严格客户信息脱敏处理。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-qa-extractor/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>legal-text-format</name>\n      <description>将法律文本（法律条文或法律案例）转换为规范的 Markdown 格式，删除推广冗余信息。本技能应在用户需要处理法律条文（如民法典、刑法等）、整理法律案例（如最高法典型案例、裁判文书等）、或从粘贴文本中格式化法律文档时使用。注意：本技能只负责格式化和内容清理，不包含内容抓取能力。内容获取应由其他 skill（如 wechat-article-fetch）完成，AI 会自动判断技能协作顺序。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/legal-text-format/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>litigation-analysis</name>\n      <description>诉讼分析工具 - 判决书深度分析，生成上诉/再审决策支持</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/litigation-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>official-document-writer</name>\n      <description>Use this skill only when the user explicitly asks to draft, polish, revise, or export a formal Chinese official document such as 请示、报告、汇报材料、公文草拟. The skill should first gather authoritative policy basis from available web search/fetch tools or user-provided/local materials, then draft the document in formal official Chinese style. Do not use this skill for general policy Q&A, legal retrieval, ordinary article writing, or broad research tasks.</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/official-document-writer/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>patent-analysis</name>\n      <description>当需要分析专利文件、进行侵权评估、提取技术特征、或比较多个专利的保护范围时使用。触发场景包括专利比对、权利要求分析、侵权检查、专利技术要点总结、专利稳定性分析、专利价值评估、FTO分析。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/patent-analysis/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>policy-rag</name>\n      <description>当用户需要处理企业内部制度文件、审批流程表、审批权责表，或需要基于内部制度与审批流进行检索、问答、索引构建时，使用本技能。适用于制度文档拆分、Excel 审批表转换、制度索引构建、制度条款检索、审批路径检索等场景。不适用于国家法律法规、司法解释、裁判案例等法律检索任务；此类问题应交由专门的法律检索技能处理。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/policy-rag/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>trademark-assistant</name>\n      <description>面向中国商标申请的类别规划、可注册性初筛及申请材料准备技能。基于尼斯分类（国际商标分类），引用中国法律法规。本技能应在接到商标咨询、需要结构化输出建议与风险分级、或需要准备申请材料时使用。不要用于：替代正式法律意见、承诺注册成功率、处理复杂商标争议案件。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/trademark-assistant/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>wechat-article-fetch</name>\n      <description>抓取微信公众号文章内容，使用 Playwright headless 模式无弹窗后台抓取，支持动态加载内容，自动提取标题和正文并保存为 Markdown 文件。本技能应在用户需要抓取微信公众号文章内容时使用。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/wechat-article-fetch/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n    <skill>\n      <name>wechat-article-search</name>\n      <description>当用户明确要求搜索微信公众号文章、公众号推文、某个公众号最近文章，或按关键词查找微信公众号文章时使用本技能。本技能通过搜狗微信搜索返回结构化文章信息，包括标题、摘要、发布时间、来源公众号和链接。</description>\n      <location>/mnt/skills/custom/policies-regulations/wechat-article-search/SKILL.md</location>\n    </skill>\n</available_skills>\n\n</skill_system>","additional_kwargs":{"message_type":"routed_skill_prompt","internal":true},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"routing_skill_guidance","id":"cc6ee8b6-0420-4f81-b1da-560f58730fdd"},{"content":"<system_reminder>\nUse the following current-turn intent and routing guidance when deciding whether to create or update todos. Treat it as planning context, not as a user request.\n<hidden_step source=\"intent_recognition\" title=\"意图识别\">\n改写后的任务：场景：政策法规。场景ID：policy_regulation\n识别场景：政策法规 (policy_regulation)；场景模式：single；候选场景：policy_regulation\n任务切分：\n- 请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。\n任务规划：\n1. 检索与解析禁停区管理规范：基于政策法规场景能力，定向检索地方性交通管理条例及交管部门关于“禁止停车区域”的认定标准与违停时间界定条款；提取核心合规依据（如连续停放阈值、临时停靠豁免条件）；输出结构化政策条文清单及关键时间参数。\n2. 构建连续性判定逻辑模型：结合目标轨迹监测特征与已提取的政策时间阈值，规划从单帧检测到时序连续性的转换规则；明确关键指标（如有效停留时长计算口径、跨帧去重机制、中断判定容差）；输出目标连续驻留的时间序列处理方案。\n3. 映射合规要求与技术判别标准：将法规中的“连续5分钟”定义与轨迹数据的时间戳连续性要求进行对齐分析；设定阶段性产出为合规判定对照表，明确满足连续违规的技术条件与排除单帧误报的过滤策略。\n4. 生成标准化合规研判流程：整合政策依据与轨迹分析逻辑，制定可执行的判定时序步骤；明确输入数据格式要求、中间校验节点及最终输出格式（合规/疑似违规/证据不足）；形成面向后续智能体调用的标准化判定SOP文档。\n场景任务：\n- policy_regulation: 我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。；参数：{'政策主题': '禁停区停车时长规定', '分析目标': '合规判断'}\n已提取参数：{'政策主题': '禁停区停车时长规定', '分析目标': '合规判断'}\n任务提示：\n- 提取必填参数：政策主题。需要查询、解读、对比或引用的政策法规主题\n- 提取可选参数：地区或层级。政策法规适用的地区、行政层级、行业领域或发布主体\n- 提取可选参数：分析目标。用户需要执行的动作，如查询条文、解释政策、合规判断、生成依据、对比差异、合同审查、法律咨询、诉讼分析、专利分析、商标申请、法律文书、公文写作等\n</hidden_step>\n</system_reminder>","additional_kwargs":{},"response_metadata":{},"type":"human","name":"todo_routing_guidance","id":"d5e64d4b-06ce-449c-b936-0c62f3531f08"},{"content":"判断目标是否**连续**5分钟出现在禁停区，核心在于从\"单帧检测\"升级为\"跨帧时序追踪\"。下面给出完整方案：\n\n---\n\n## 一、判定逻辑框架\n\n| 判定维度 | 关键要点 |\n|---------|---------|\n| **时间连续性** | 目标ID在相邻帧之间不断裂（同一目标不被误拆或误合并） |\n| **空间一致性** | 目标始终位于禁停区的地理围栏内 |\n| **有效停留时长** | 累计 ≥ 300秒（可设容差 ±N 秒） |\n| **中断判定** | 目标消失超过容差阈值后重新出现 → 视为中断，时间重置 |\n\n---\n\n## 二、具体实施步骤\n\n### 第1步：获取带时间戳的轨迹数据\n\n通过视频分析工具对禁停区域进行持续检测/追踪，输出每帧中目标的：\n\n- **唯一目标ID**（track ID）\n- **中心坐标**（判断是否在禁停区内）\n- **时间戳**（精确到秒）\n- **置信度**（过滤低质量检测）\n\n### 第2步：计算连续停留时长\n\n```\n伪代码逻辑：\n1. 按目标ID分组所有检测记录\n2. 对每个目标ID的记录按时间戳排序\n3. 遍历记录，检查相邻帧的时间间隔 Δt：\n   - 如果 Δt ≤ 容差阈值（如 3~5 秒）→ 属于同一段连续停留\n   - 如果 Δt > 容差阈值 → 前一段结束，新的一段开始\n4. 累加每段的有效停留总时长\n5. 如果任一段 ≥ 300秒 → 判定为\"连续5分钟违规\"\n```\n\n### 第3步：容差设计\n\n为避免短暂信号丢失导致误判，建议设置：\n\n- **最大允许中断时间**：3~5秒（即目标短暂被遮挡后恢复仍可算作连续）\n- **最低检测频率**：至少每秒1帧以上\n- **置信度下限**：剔除置信度过低的误检\n\n---\n\n## 三、技术实现方式\n\n如果你有**视频文件**，我可以直接使用视频分析工具进行检测和追踪：\n\n> **需要提供：** 视频文件路径\n\n如果你有**已检测出的结构化数据**（CSV/Excel），我也可以帮你做时序分析：\n\n> **需要提供：** 包含目标ID、时间戳、坐标的数据文件\n\n---\n\n## 四、输出结果格式\n\n最终输出类似：\n\n```\n目标ID: TRACK_007\n首次出现: 2026-07-23 10:15:22\n末次出现: 2026-07-23 10:21:48\n中间是否有中断: 否（最大空档 2秒）\n连续停留时长: 386秒\n判定结论: ✅ 连续5分钟出现在禁停区（违规）\n```\n\n---\n\n**请告诉我你目前有什么类型的数据？** 是视频文件、检测结果的CSV/Excel，还是其他格式？我会根据实际数据给出具体的分析操作。","additional_kwargs":{"refusal":null},"response_metadata":{"token_usage":{"completion_tokens":934,"prompt_tokens":13132,"total_tokens":14066,"completion_tokens_details":{"accepted_prediction_tokens":null,"audio_tokens":null,"reasoning_tokens":234,"rejected_prediction_tokens":null,"text_tokens":934},"prompt_tokens_details":{"audio_tokens":null,"cached_tokens":null,"text_tokens":13132}},"model_provider":"openai","model_name":"qwen3.6-35b-a3b","system_fingerprint":null,"id":"chatcmpl-2263e145-85e9-9633-ad64-45492bf75d4b","finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null},"type":"ai","name":null,"id":"lc_run--019f8f79-67d6-77b0-9136-66a9b8bd2b76-0","tool_calls":[],"invalid_tool_calls":[],"usage_metadata":{"input_tokens":13132,"output_tokens":934,"total_tokens":14066,"input_token_details":{},"output_token_details":{"reasoning":234}}}],"viewed_images":{},"intent_context":{"intent":"task","original_query":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","normalized_query":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","routing_query":"场景：政策法规。场景ID：policy_regulation。场景说明：政策、法规、制度、条例、通知、合规依据、法律条文查询与解读，以及中国法律咨询、合同审查、诉讼分析、专利商标、法律文书、公文写作、微信公众号法律文章检索和企业内部制度检索场景。需要识别参数：政策主题、地区或层级、分析目标。用户原始问题：我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现","scene":"policy_regulation","scene_name":"政策法规","params":{"政策主题":"禁停区停车时长规定","分析目标":"合规判断"},"scene_mode":"single","scenes":["policy_regulation"],"task_spans":[{"task_span_id":"span_78924c","text":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。"}],"planning_steps":[{"task_span_id":"span_4c821c","text":"检索与解析禁停区管理规范：基于政策法规场景能力，定向检索地方性交通管理条例及交管部门关于“禁止停车区域”的认定标准与违停时间界定条款；提取核心合规依据（如连续停放阈值、临时停靠豁免条件）；输出结构化政策条文清单及关键时间参数。"},{"task_span_id":"span_e47f29","text":"构建连续性判定逻辑模型：结合目标轨迹监测特征与已提取的政策时间阈值，规划从单帧检测到时序连续性的转换规则；明确关键指标（如有效停留时长计算口径、跨帧去重机制、中断判定容差）；输出目标连续驻留的时间序列处理方案。"},{"task_span_id":"span_095ad5","text":"映射合规要求与技术判别标准：将法规中的“连续5分钟”定义与轨迹数据的时间戳连续性要求进行对齐分析；设定阶段性产出为合规判定对照表，明确满足连续违规的技术条件与排除单帧误报的过滤策略。"},{"task_span_id":"span_26c0db","text":"生成标准化合规研判流程：整合政策依据与轨迹分析逻辑，制定可执行的判定时序步骤；明确输入数据格式要求、中间校验节点及最终输出格式（合规/疑似违规/证据不足）；形成面向后续智能体调用的标准化判定SOP文档。"}],"scene_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_258f29","scene":"policy_regulation","scene_name":"政策法规","text":"我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","params":{"政策主题":"禁停区停车时长规定","分析目标":"合规判断"}}],"sub_tasks":[{"sub_task_id":"sub_258f29","scene":"policy_regulation","scene_name":"政策法规","text":"我将根据政策法规中禁停区停车时长规定的合规判断要求，判定目标是否连续5分钟出现在禁停区而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","params":{"政策主题":"禁停区停车时长规定","分析目标":"合规判断"}}],"task_hints":["提取必填参数：政策主题。需要查询、解读、对比或引用的政策法规主题","提取可选参数：地区或层级。政策法规适用的地区、行政层级、行业领域或发布主体","提取可选参数：分析目标。用户需要执行的动作，如查询条文、解释政策、合规判断、生成依据、对比差异、合同审查、法律咨询、诉讼分析、专利分析、商标申请、法律文书、公文写作等"],"mentioned_skill_ids":[],"confidence":0.9,"reason":"llm_scene_slot_rewrite","_source_message_key":"id:d7d8f4ef-6fb1-449d-95f4-d11cfedf7409"},"routing_context":{"route_mode":"scene_filter","trigger":true,"primary_goal":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","scene_tasks":[{"scene_task_id":"task_001","segment_id":"seg_001","segment_text":"请判断某个目标是否连续 5 分钟出现在禁停区，而不是只在单帧中短暂出现。","scene":"policy_regulation","input_refs":[],"task_types":[],"selected_skills":[{"id":"china-contract-review","role":"primary","score":1.0,"re